d dtype-independent gap showed. Replacing key construction, two dict lookups, device-index access and wrapper frames with a cached integer-address launch closure removed roughly half of that gap; what remains is the irreducible allocation (5.5 us) plus compiled-launch (8.3 us) floor, which the reference pays too.", "round_num": 2, "strategy_evolution": "Round 1 measured the seed and separated a host-side limit (nine workloads) from a device-side limit (three workloads). Round 2 fixed the host side only, keeping the kernel byte-identical so the effect was attributable. The device limit is now the largest remaining term and becomes the next target.", "watching": "none"}}
